<title>FRANCE: Elf shares placed at 417.50 ffr/shr. [CORRECTED 11:35 GMT]</title>
<headline>Elf shares placed at 417.50 ffr/shr. [CORRECTED 11:35 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Finance Minister Jean Arthuis said in a statement that the state had sold 12,584,240 shares in oil group Elf Aquitaine at a price of 417.50 francs per share.  </p>
<p>He said in a statement that the placement, conducted by Paribas and SBC Warburg (corrects name of second broker from Goldman Sachs), &quot;was a great success and closed in the middle of the morning.&quot;</p>
<p>The placement was with French and international institutional investors.</p>
</text>
